+| Publication consulted | Source location | Decision informed |
+|---|---|---|
+| Broadcom Product Interoperability Matrix | https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Solution | Consulted the live interoperability authority for the VCF 9.1 target combination. Because matrix results are mutable and selected interactively, the generated component versions remain pinned to the supplied compatibility snapshot. |
+| “Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1” (Broadcom KB 440630) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html | Confirmed that VCF 5.2.x estates use the VCF 9.1 lifecycle path, that VCF Operations precedes the core lifecycle workflow, and that license readiness is a migration gate. |
+| “Update Sequence for VCF 9.0 and Compatible VMware Products” (Broadcom KB 390634) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390634/update-sequence-for-vcf-90-and-compatibl.html | Confirmed the core dependency direction: management services/SDDC Manager, NSX, vCenter, ESXi, then vSAN disk-format work. This informed the dependency-valid ordering in the plan. |
+| “vCenter and vRNI Report 100% NSX-T Edge CPU Utilization but Edge vCPUs are not fully utilized” (Broadcom KB 329045) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/329045/vcenter-and-vrni-report-100-nsxt-edge-cp.html | Confirmed the 4/8/16-vCPU Medium/Large/XL Edge resource progression. The pinned throughput bands select XLARGE for the required 18 Gbps on the sole surviving Edge. |
+| “Unable to change MTU on Edge fp-eth interfaces in VCF 9” (Broadcom KB 422523) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/422523/unable-to-change-mtu-on-edge-fpeth-inter.html | Confirmed that VCF 9 Edge deployment uses the multiple-TEP uplink profile and the global fabric MTU, supporting the dual-uplink, 9000-MTU TEP design. |
+
+No live source consulted exposed a value that conflicted with `authority/compatibility-snapshot.json`; generated artifacts therefore retain every pinned value.
